der_own":false,"_score_insider_own":17.2,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Valmont Industries, Inc. operates as a manufacturer of products and services for infrastructure and agriculture markets in the United States, Australia, Brazil, and internationally. The company operates in two segments, Infrastructure and Agriculture. It manufactures and distributes steel, pre-stressed concrete, composite structures for electrical transmission, substation, and distribution applications; and designs, engineers, and manufactures metal, steel, wood, aluminum, and composite poles and structures for lighting and transportation applications. The company also offers galvanizing and painting, and powder coating services for paint products; towers, small cell structures, camouflage concealment solutions, passive intermodulation mitigation equipment, and components for wireless communication markets; and solar single-axis tracker product, an integrated system of steel structures, electric motors, and electronic controllers, as well as provides coatings services to protect metal products. In addition, it manufactures center pivot components and linear irrigation equipment for the agricultural markets, such as parts and tubular products for industrial customers; advanced technology solutions for agricultural sector; mechanical irrigation equipment and service parts under the Valley brand name. Valmont Industries, Inc. was founded in 1946 and is headquartered in Omaha, Nebraska.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Avner M. Applbaum CPA | CEO, President & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $380K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Valmont Industries, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $8.1B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The business throws off $311M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.30\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 10.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 3.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.013331723279087875},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Valmont Industries Inc. (VMI) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/81/Precision_Trading_with_Valmont_Industries_Inc._VMI_Risk_Zones_110426054402_1793789042.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793789042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Agriculture Stocks To Keep An Eye On \u2013 November 12th","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/agriculture-stocks-to-keep-an-eye-on-november-12th.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794510932.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Agriculture Stocks To Consider \u2013 November 11th","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/agriculture-stocks-to-consider-november-11th.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794424622.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Agriculture Stocks To Consider \u2013 November 7th","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/agriculture-stocks-to-consider-november-7th.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794305553.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Fortune Brands Elects Victor Grizzle to Board of Directors","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://fina